    LLM: "Game: Gong Zhu (Chase the Pig). 4-5 players. Setup: Deal 13 cards (4-player) or 10 cards (5-player, remove 2â™£ 2â™¦). Before play: Expose optional cards (Aâ™¥, Qâ™ , Jâ™¦, 10â™£) to double their values (quadruple for 10â™£). Play: Holder of 2â™  leads; play tricks following suit. Scoring: Penalty cards taken count against you (-100 Qâ™ , -50 Aâ™¥, -40 Kâ™¥, etc.). Bonuses: Jâ™¦=+100, 10â™£=+50 alone or doubles all other scoring. Taking all hearts=+200. Game ends when player reaches -1000 (the 'pig', loser).",
    Player: "Welcome to Gong Zhu (Chase the Pig), the Chinese card game! Before play, you may expose penalty cards (Aâ™¥, Qâ™ ) or bonus cards (Jâ™¦, 10â™£) to double their values. Play tricks avoiding penalties: Qâ™ =-100, Aâ™¥=-50, Kâ™¥=-40, etc. Jack of Diamonds=+100! Ten of Clubs doubles all your other scoring cards. The first player to reach -1000 becomes the 'pig' and loses. Or try to take ALL hearts for +200 bonus!",
    objective: 'Avoid taking penalty cards (hearts and Queen of Spades). Collect the Jack of Diamonds for a bonus. The Ten of Clubs doubles all your scoring cards if you take any other scoring card, or scores +50 alone.',
    gameplay: '1. Before play, players may expose certain cards to double their values\n2. Holder of 2â™  leads first hand; thereafter, holder of Qâ™  (pig) from previous hand leads\n3. Any card may be led (no restriction on hearts/spades)\n4. Must follow suit if possible; may play any card if cannot follow\n5. Highest card of led suit wins trick\n6. Winner leads to next trick',
